# TurboMCP plugin: ignore build output, keep source.
#
# The plugin is source-only. A project that wants it compiles it, so compiler
# output and IDE files are never committed.

# Unreal build output
Binaries/
Intermediate/
Build/
DerivedDataCache/

# Visual Studio
.vs/
*.sln
*.suo
*.opensdf
*.sdf
*.VC.db
*.VC.opendb

# JetBrains
.idea/

# The agent's working notes and engine reference copies are local scratch,
# not part of the plugin.
.agent/

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Python bytecode from the Tools scripts
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Commit-message files are a workflow artefact, not part of the plugin.
.commit-msg*.txt

# A compiled binary that reads the Windows Credential Manager must never be committed.
# The source it is built from is local too; see the note in Tools/README.md.
GitCredentialHelper*
*.exe

# Temporary commit-message files. They were written by the agent that made these commits and one
# of them reached a commit because its name did not match the existing pattern.
.cmsg*.txt
*.cmsg.txt

# Local feedback notes: not part of the plugin, never pushed.
Feedbacks/
